{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"Top strengths: The concept is very legible: AI agents as a literal review bench is a strong founder/operator metaphor, and using video-claw’s $0 TTS to narrate its own demo is clean “medium is the message” storytelling. The plan is also executable: concrete shots, durations, file paths, and verification steps give a worker enough structure to render a first cut.\n\nRisks/gaps: The final ffmpeg command uses `-shortest`; because VO likely ends before the 55s video, the render may truncate the final pull-back. Add silence/apad or remove `-shortest`. The zoompan/concat path needs stricter normalization: add `setsar=1`, consistent timebase/fps, and consider concat filter if the demuxer produces DTS/timebase issues. The audio plan is underbuilt: separate TTS lines at fixed offsets may overlap or feel mistimed, and there is no loudness normalization, room tone, music bed, or ducking pass.\n\nDesign improvements: Make the “peer review” visible as verdict marks or projected annotations between tribes, not just hallway tension. Also consider a sharper final reversal: the VP silhouette approves, then we reveal the “founder” is alone at the table while the agent bench keeps moving.\n\n- Codex"}}
